                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c61701b-307e-452a-9f29-c7f2a23eb724",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd797381-747c-3a35-9e04-1992ca57e125",
                        "target_lang_word": "sanctimonious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sanctimonious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a84cdf18-e6d1-3a70-bb58-d4ce9c8f8664",
                                        "entry_id": "85a02284-ba49-385c-ae23-93dd81668fbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Making a show of being morally better than others, especially hypocritically pious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0294fa28-0752-456b-acf3-2e63f7537794",
                                                "sense_id": "a84cdf18-e6d1-3a70-bb58-d4ce9c8f8664",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: smug; see also Thesaurus:arrogant"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e251ecf6-3516-457f-9ac8-9e1ea5214cef",
                                                "sense_id": "a84cdf18-e6d1-3a70-bb58-d4ce9c8f8664",
                                                "text": "Thou conclud'st like the sanctimonious pirate, that went to sea with the Ten Commandements, but scrap'd one out of the table."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71aa4e45-c0a3-46a6-9545-488c5f7bde66",
                                                "sense_id": "a84cdf18-e6d1-3a70-bb58-d4ce9c8f8664",
                                                "text": "[O]ne / Discuss'd his tutor, rough to common men / But honeying at the whisper of a lord; / And one the Master, as a rogue in grain / Veneer'd with sanctimonious theory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd8b738f-2243-49c2-b5b8-df093be9aed1",
                                                "sense_id": "a84cdf18-e6d1-3a70-bb58-d4ce9c8f8664",
                                                "text": "It'd be easy to write off Michael Moore as a fat, scruffy, sanctimonious Bolchevik poseur (actually, I do write off Michael Moore as a fat, scruffy, sanctimonious Bolchevik poseur) but the fact is that there's about five minutes of cleverness in this […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56c35dae-20e7-4df4-b94e-baddafabe2eb",
                                                "sense_id": "a84cdf18-e6d1-3a70-bb58-d4ce9c8f8664",
                                                "text": "And this is indeed needed, since we who consider these awkward Christian ideas are but fearful, sanctimonious people, as Kierkegaard once put it so passionately: O, you sanctimonious people with your love which does not set you apart […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e72cef45-b80d-3ca9-81c8-a8c18c163b63",
                                        "entry_id": "85a02284-ba49-385c-ae23-93dd81668fbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Holy, devout."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "83ef7051-f490-4523-a283-50b5f530b53a",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd797381-747c-3a35-9e04-1992ca57e125",
                        "target_lang_word": "holier-than-thou",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "holier-than-thou",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                        "entry_id": "72635ac1-d7b9-3793-bbd0-e2e637051598",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hypocritically or self-righteously pious; sanctimonious; smugly morally superior."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa710981-9a6d-414e-80a5-f1eceb132bff",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "[T]here are local jealousies and disunities which are not likely to be soothed by the patent fact that companies which most strenuously assert the I-am-holier-than-thou claim daily violate the rules by which they profess to be invariably governed, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c6951a3-780f-4eca-a7dd-35504a2e0f6f",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "Hippolytus is quite insufferable in his endless protestations of pity and purity. One tires of such abnormal goodness and wishes for a little natural depravity. He is a perfect type of the \"holier than thou\" individual whose secret heart is a very stagnation of egotism, selfishness and disregard for others' feelings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "056adba3-335a-4f87-9e47-1acdd20d3a30",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "His garb is such as any gentleman might wear—a farmer, a thrifty mechanic, a teacher, or a plain business man—a brown slouch hat, any kind of a simple necktie, any kind of a coat except the unctuous holier-than-thou broadcloth with the front full of button holes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8454d0d9-204c-41b0-adc8-cb41f258690a",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "I don't think the \"black is white\" campaign of the Republican Party is going to succeed. I think the voters are going to see through this holier-than-thou disguise that our Republican friends are putting on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "846bea4e-4795-4c21-82cc-a2fa9d55000f",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "But I can understand the hon. member's sense of sanctimony; he has now been a member of the NDP caucus for a while and the holier-than-thou attitude has been bred into him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "879c02a4-180f-45ef-b594-b3aebc36631f",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "The Soviet economy is hurting now, and I say that not holier-than-thou, but it is; factually, the Soviet economy is in bad shape."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00f24a21-f0cf-432c-86ef-5910de72928c",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "Whether you see that as belated recognition of a collective shame (if not guilt) or as a \"holier than thou\" pharisaism, it was certainly made much simpler by the fact that the generation under discussion had started to fade from public life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c76ef47-5a35-460a-a450-6096501c5264",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "Everything connected with the care of children no matter how trivial has to be seen to be politically correct. This tends to create a \"holier-than-thou\" attitude, where if something even hints of being politically incorrect, then no matter how much fun it might be for the children, it will not take place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05d88ec7-256b-4bfc-95e3-00e7b7c381d2",
                                                "sense_id": "1108efb3-2457-3cb0-af73-a2de61dd1b6d",
                                                "text": "While he may not deserve to be branded a “slimeball,” as Trump did on Sunday, Comey does risk coming across as a disgruntled ex-employee and someone seeking vengeance for his dismissal. He has a highly developed sense of his own morality and sometimes comes across as holier than thou."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0e23ac58-f91c-41f6-97d2-49f8c2d34c87",
